- [Kelly] He takes more
time than I do, probably.

00:07:06.340 --> 00:07:07.173
- [Terry] Yeah. I know.

00:07:07.173 --> 00:07:08.360
- Which the bar is low.

00:07:08.360 --> 00:07:11.380
But yeah, he's really into it as well.

00:07:11.380 --> 00:07:13.430
I know a lot of men are
like way more into fashion

00:07:13.430 --> 00:07:14.263
than women I know.

00:07:14.263 --> 00:07:15.588
- [Terry] But see, we could
take care of ourselves now.

00:07:15.588 --> 00:07:16.857
- [Simon] Oh, I'm obsessed with it

00:07:16.857 --> 00:07:17.690
- You are?

00:07:17.690 --> 00:07:18.523
- Oh, look at me.

00:07:18.523 --> 00:07:19.356
- I was like your black
shirts, and your...

00:07:19.356 --> 00:07:22.406
I was gonna go for the
joke, but you did first.

00:07:22.406 --> 00:07:24.013
- Oh, no, no, trust me.

00:07:24.013 --> 00:07:25.573
It's like, what are you
gonna wear next week?

00:07:25.573 --> 00:07:27.210
It's like, the same.

00:07:27.210 --> 00:07:28.155
- [Kelly] The Johnny Cash black.

00:07:28.155 --> 00:07:29.313
- I just have one outfit.

00:07:29.313 --> 00:07:30.522
- [Kelly] You know what? It's nice.

00:07:30.522 --> 00:07:31.393
- It's easy.

00:07:31.393 --> 00:07:32.560
- You don't have to think about it.

00:07:32.560 --> 00:07:33.393
- Exactly.

00:07:33.393 --> 00:07:36.838
- Exactly. I look the same
unless Candace is styling me.

00:07:36.838 --> 00:07:38.233
I'm with you, jeans, tee shirt.

00:07:38.233 --> 00:07:41.200
- Meanwhile, Heidi and I,
when we have to repeat clothes

00:07:41.200 --> 00:07:43.355
because of the auditions,
we don't like it.

00:07:43.355 --> 00:07:44.188
- Again!

00:07:44.188 --> 00:07:45.604
- We're like, we don't
wanna work anymore here,

00:07:45.604 --> 00:07:49.361
wearing the same outfit
for two days in a row.

00:07:49.361 --> 00:07:50.194
- I think this is the hardest for us,

00:07:50.194 --> 00:07:52.191
because sometimes we are like,
five days in the same look,

00:07:52.191 --> 00:07:54.780
and honestly the outfit
can walk by itself.

00:07:54.780 --> 00:07:55.870
We're always talking to one another.

00:07:55.870 --> 00:07:58.200
We're like, "Again, the same outfit!"

00:07:58.200 --> 00:07:59.040
- You hate it.

00:07:59.040 --> 00:08:00.930
- [Kelly] That's actually
happened to me on a show!

00:08:00.930 --> 00:08:01.877
You have to wear it for
like five days in a row.

00:08:01.877 --> 00:08:04.020
And it's like, you have
to be very specific

00:08:04.020 --> 00:08:05.750
about what you're wearing,
because especially

00:08:05.750 --> 00:08:09.340
if it's stretchy at all,
like elasticity wears.

00:08:09.340 --> 00:08:11.043
And so like by day five...

00:08:11.043 --> 00:08:12.430
- It's a complete different dress,

00:08:12.430 --> 00:08:13.780
that happens to me all the time.

00:08:13.780 --> 00:08:14.970
I sit down for three days,

00:08:14.970 --> 00:08:16.380
and then it's like, "What is this?"

00:08:16.380 --> 00:08:18.697
It's like, "Oh no, now you
have to do the red carpet."

00:08:18.697 --> 00:08:20.489
I'm like, I just can't, I can't.

00:08:20.489 --> 00:08:22.610
- [Kelly] No, and it stretches as well.

00:08:22.610 --> 00:08:24.030
It's like, especially if,
if it's like a jumpsuit,

00:08:24.030 --> 00:08:25.380
I did a jumpsuit one time and I was like,

00:08:25.380 --> 00:08:27.570
how is this elongated, like it's longer?

00:08:27.570 --> 00:08:29.960
And I'm so short, we
just cut the bottom line.

00:08:29.960 --> 00:08:30.907
Yeah, it's really hard.

00:08:30.907 --> 00:08:32.610
- All of a sudden, it's a drop-crotch.

00:08:32.610 --> 00:08:33.820
- Yeah, I'm just all of a sudden,

00:08:33.820 --> 00:08:36.020
which is not attractive
on a person that's 5'3".

00:08:36.020 --> 00:08:37.520
- [Simon] We could have uniforms.

00:08:37.520 --> 00:08:38.369
- Yeah, you just look shorter.

00:08:38.369 --> 00:08:39.318
No, we don't want uniforms.

00:08:39.318 --> 00:08:40.897
- Look what he's saying,
that we should wear uniforms.

00:08:40.897 --> 00:08:42.426
- [Simon] Yes, it's easy!

00:08:42.426 --> 00:08:43.723
- [Terry] AGT uniforms.

00:08:43.723 --> 00:08:45.527
- No, no, no.

00:08:45.527 --> 00:08:49.230
- Honestly, I am actually
gonna side with Simon on this

00:08:49.230 --> 00:08:51.131
'cause it'd be way easier.

00:08:51.131 --> 00:08:52.250
- You might like them.

00:08:52.250 --> 00:08:53.503
- A nice AGT uniform.

00:08:53.503 --> 00:08:55.601
You wear "A", I wear "G", you wear "T".

00:08:55.601 --> 00:08:56.511
- [Simon] Yes, yes!

00:08:56.511 --> 00:08:57.344
- [Sofia] No!

00:08:57.344 --> 00:09:00.003
- Heidi, at least we can
swap our uniforms, at least.

00:09:01.640 --> 00:09:03.190
- Just let us do it for one day, please.

00:09:03.190 --> 00:09:05.218
- [Kelly] It will not, look
at her face. She just said no.

00:09:05.218 --> 00:09:06.870
- Only if you let me
dress you for one day.

00:09:06.870 --> 00:09:07.943
- [Simon] Okay, done, deal.

00:09:07.943 --> 00:09:09.273
- [Kelly] (gasps) Oh my God.

00:09:12.644 --> 00:09:14.820
- You have to keep this promise.

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:16.753
- Why are you agreeing without my consent?

00:09:16.753 --> 00:09:20.700
- [Heidi] We'll do it together,
we go shopping together.

00:09:20.700 --> 00:09:22.060
We hook him up with a new outfit.

00:09:22.060 --> 00:09:23.870
- Oh, okay, that's what that was.

00:09:23.870 --> 00:09:27.020
- Yeah, you get to dress him
and he gets to dress y'all.

00:09:27.020 --> 00:09:28.533
This should be interesting.

00:09:28.533 --> 00:09:29.376
- I thought it was like a uniform.

00:09:29.376 --> 00:09:30.350
- This one right here!

00:09:30.350 --> 00:09:31.210
- What are you gonna wear?

00:09:31.210 --> 00:09:32.150
You have to do something,

00:09:32.150 --> 00:09:34.160
this is not just a bet
that you get scot-free.

00:09:34.160 --> 00:09:35.900
- I'm going shirtless,
I'm going shirtless.

00:09:35.900 --> 00:09:37.383
- [Sofia] Yeah, so that
you can go with everything.

00:09:37.383 --> 00:09:38.466
- [Kelly] That's where we all win.

00:09:38.466 --> 00:09:39.314
- It always matches.

00:09:39.314 --> 00:09:41.360
Everything matches with shirtless.

00:09:41.360 --> 00:09:42.383
- Everyone wins, everything wins.

00:09:42.383 --> 00:09:45.473
So who takes the longest
in hair and makeup?

00:09:45.473 --> 00:09:46.369
(Simon clears his throat)

00:09:46.369 --> 00:09:47.495
- [Terry] Ooh.

00:09:47.495 --> 00:09:49.170
- Oh, nobody even thought about it.

00:09:49.170 --> 00:09:50.003
- [Simon] Oh, come on.

00:09:50.003 --> 00:09:51.682
- To be honest, to be
honest, we never stop.

00:09:51.682 --> 00:09:53.140
- Well, we never stop.

00:09:53.140 --> 00:09:54.933
But the thing is that there's
always something happens

00:09:54.933 --> 00:09:57.724
to me because I am Latin, it is true.

00:09:57.724 --> 00:09:59.521
I always wake up on-time.

00:09:59.521 --> 00:10:01.760
It's not that I'm sleeping or anything.

00:10:01.760 --> 00:10:04.090
I wake up on time, but
something always happens

00:10:04.090 --> 00:10:07.500
and I'm always not in the
perfect, perfect time.

00:10:07.500 --> 00:10:09.440
She, you are always in the perfect time.

00:10:09.440 --> 00:10:10.950
- I think it's because you wear one lens

00:10:10.950 --> 00:10:13.510
and not in the other,
so you're always like...

00:10:13.510 --> 00:10:17.710
- I don't know, but there's
always something or I fall down

00:10:18.570 --> 00:10:19.938
- It's because of one lens!

00:10:19.938 --> 00:10:20.900
- Or I can't find the eyeliner,

00:10:20.900 --> 00:10:23.990
or the dog is doing something
it's not supposed to do,

00:10:23.990 --> 00:10:25.522
oh, there's always some drama in my house.

00:10:25.522 --> 00:10:27.820
- [Simon] So basically,
the answer is Sofía.

00:10:27.820 --> 00:10:30.919
- So let's talk about the
new season of the show.

00:10:30.919 --> 00:10:34.274
So Simon, what act on America's Got Talent

00:10:34.274 --> 00:10:36.350
has scared you the most,
of all the seasons?

00:10:36.350 --> 00:10:37.671
- Ooh. Oh, I know.

00:10:37.671 --> 00:10:38.510
- Two.

00:10:38.510 --> 00:10:39.343
- Okay.

00:10:39.343 --> 00:10:42.551
- Two people went up a
very, very, very high pole.

00:10:42.551 --> 00:10:43.384
- [Terry] Oh!

00:10:43.384 --> 00:10:45.984
- I mean, it, it's difficult to describe,

00:10:45.984 --> 00:10:49.292
but it was very scary
and it nearly went wrong,

00:10:49.292 --> 00:10:51.320
and it was a father and a daughter,

00:10:51.320 --> 00:10:54.338
and they're like 300
feet, 400 feet in the air.

00:10:54.338 --> 00:10:57.800
One of then's blindfolded,
and then she got nervous.

00:10:57.800 --> 00:10:59.820
- Did something happen to the dad? Or no?

00:10:59.820 --> 00:11:03.050
- [Simon] It was just, it, it
nearly went horribly wrong.

00:11:03.050 --> 00:11:04.690
So it was terrifying, and in fact,

00:11:04.690 --> 00:11:06.652
I asked them the question
because they were so high up,

00:11:06.652 --> 00:11:08.663
I said, what, what happened?

00:11:08.663 --> 00:11:12.680
And basically she lost
her nerve at the top,

00:11:12.680 --> 00:11:15.417
and she's talking to her dad
and her dad's basically saying,

00:11:15.417 --> 00:11:17.345
"Look, maybe we shouldn't do this."

00:11:17.345 --> 00:11:19.450
So it was terrifying.

00:11:19.450 --> 00:11:23.060
And the second most terrifying was a girl

00:11:23.060 --> 00:11:25.084
who was 10 years old.

00:11:25.084 --> 00:11:25.917
- Yes.

00:11:25.917 --> 00:11:27.490
- I won't give it away, but I thought

00:11:27.490 --> 00:11:30.930
she was very sweet until
she started to sing.

00:11:30.930 --> 00:11:34.063
And it, and I actually
called for a priest.

00:11:34.953 --> 00:11:36.612
- [Kelly] It was like the Exorcist?

00:11:36.612 --> 00:11:38.044
- [Simon] It was like the Exorcist.

00:11:38.044 --> 00:11:39.436
- Was she into like heavy metal?

00:11:39.436 --> 00:11:40.730
- It was crazy.

00:11:40.730 --> 00:11:43.450
- It was, I'll actually send you the clip,

00:11:43.450 --> 00:11:45.867
because I, that was my
expression, I'm like, what?

00:11:45.867 --> 00:11:46.700
And I asked her,

00:11:46.700 --> 00:11:48.070
"Have you ever seen a
movie called the Exorcist?"

00:11:48.070 --> 00:11:50.040
And she just stared at me.

00:11:50.040 --> 00:11:52.840
And I said, I'm not asking anything else.

00:11:52.840 --> 00:11:53.930
- She's got a voodoo doll.

00:11:53.930 --> 00:11:55.271
- I also love Jack the Whipper.

00:11:55.271 --> 00:11:56.487
- Oh my God.

00:11:56.487 --> 00:11:58.070
- You did you say "Jack The Whipper?"

00:11:58.070 --> 00:12:00.519
- Yeah, because Simon,
there's this guy with a whip,

00:12:00.519 --> 00:12:01.479
- That sounds like an S&amp;M kinda, like.

00:12:01.479 --> 00:12:05.170
- But, Simon was nice
enough to go onto the stage

00:12:05.170 --> 00:12:06.188
where we kind of made him.

00:12:06.188 --> 00:12:07.030
- You pushed me.

00:12:07.030 --> 00:12:08.220
- We pushed you.

00:12:08.220 --> 00:12:10.130
He had a stick in between his legs.

00:12:10.130 --> 00:12:12.098
He's standing there and a
skiing downhill position,

00:12:12.098 --> 00:12:15.303
and he's whipping in between
his legs, this little stick.

00:12:15.303 --> 00:12:18.350
And you know that could've
gone awfully wrong.

00:12:18.350 --> 00:12:19.183
- [Sofía] But why, it was so funny?

00:12:19.183 --> 00:12:21.050
We don't understand why it was so funny.

00:12:21.050 --> 00:12:23.303
We were down there on
the desk, like, dying.

00:12:23.303 --> 00:12:24.136
- Oh, they were loving it.

00:12:24.136 --> 00:12:26.866
- That's 'cause your body
parts aren't about to go down.

00:12:26.866 --> 00:12:28.546
- [Simon] Yeah, they
were laughing so much.

00:12:28.546 --> 00:12:31.052
I nearly have my what's-its whipped off,

00:12:31.052 --> 00:12:32.950
and they're in hysterical laughter.

00:12:32.950 --> 00:12:35.610
- I got five wrinkles more that day

00:12:35.610 --> 00:12:37.004
because we were laughing so hard.

00:12:37.004 --> 00:12:39.140
- [Kelly] Oh my God,
that's a lot of trust.

00:12:39.140 --> 00:12:40.550
I don't love, I was never good at like,

00:12:40.550 --> 00:12:42.590
the trust fall scenario,
you know when they do it?

00:12:42.590 --> 00:12:44.430
- I got my revenge, don't
worry, later on that night.

00:12:44.430 --> 00:12:46.240
- I had an apple shot off my head before

00:12:46.240 --> 00:12:48.147
with a bow and arrow, that was crazy, too.

00:12:48.147 --> 00:12:50.151
- [Kelly] Do you have to
sign some kind of waiver?

00:12:50.151 --> 00:12:51.487
Like I'm like, this seems...

00:12:51.487 --> 00:12:53.103
- No, no, but this is the funny thing.

00:12:53.103 --> 00:12:56.670
The producers are the ones
screaming at us to go up.

00:12:56.670 --> 00:13:00.240
So we've had knives
thrown at us, as you said,

00:13:00.240 --> 00:13:03.175
bolts, you know, what was it?

00:13:03.175 --> 00:13:04.850
- Like a bow and arrow.

00:13:04.850 --> 00:13:05.683
- [Simon] Bow and arrow.

00:13:05.683 --> 00:13:06.516
- [Kelly] I saw that.

00:13:06.516 --> 00:13:09.457
- Whipping, I mean, and
it's like, thanks a lot.

00:13:11.030 --> 00:13:12.340
- Do the producers like y'all?

00:13:12.340 --> 00:13:15.480
- [Heidi] You guys think
this judging stuff is easy.

00:13:15.480 --> 00:13:16.644
It's dangerous!

00:13:16.644 --> 00:13:17.477
- [Simon] It's very scary.

00:13:17.477 --> 00:13:18.310
- [Kelly] I know, I'm just saying somebody

00:13:18.310 --> 00:13:20.400
could shout that out to
me and I'd be like, nope.

00:13:20.400 --> 00:13:21.615
- [Sofía] I thought I
was not gonna make it

00:13:21.615 --> 00:13:22.770
yesterday, actually.

00:13:22.770 --> 00:13:23.603
- [Heidi] Yeah. It's true.

00:13:23.603 --> 00:13:28.047
- I thought, but you know, I
look at his face and you think,

00:13:28.047 --> 00:13:30.510
"Okay, he's the boss,
so his face, he knows,

00:13:30.510 --> 00:13:32.580
and there's no not danger."

00:13:32.580 --> 00:13:35.190
And I look at his face and
he's looking at me like...

00:13:37.682 --> 00:13:38.832
I was like, wait, wait!

00:13:42.039 --> 00:13:44.533
- [Terry] She had whips
going all around her,

00:13:46.334 --> 00:13:48.393
- [Kelly] What're you, like,
Indiana Jones on your show?

00:13:48.393 --> 00:13:49.226
- Yeah.

00:13:49.226 --> 00:13:51.520
- And you know, they get kind of nervous.

00:13:51.520 --> 00:13:55.443
So whatever they prepared, it
can go wrong, Kelly, you know?

00:13:55.443 --> 00:13:58.210
- [Sofía] But wait, what happened was also

00:13:58.210 --> 00:14:00.977
that in the middle of his
thing, he decides to put the.

00:14:00.977 --> 00:14:01.870
- [Heidi] The buzzer!

00:14:01.870 --> 00:14:04.324
- [Terry] Oh, and he shakes
the guy up, he's like, oh.

00:14:04.324 --> 00:14:07.050
- [Sofía] When you're next
to the guy, you can feel

00:14:07.050 --> 00:14:11.524
the guy's energy changing,
so I'm looking at him,

00:14:11.524 --> 00:14:14.280
I'm like, "How do I get outta here now?"

00:14:14.280 --> 00:14:16.083
Because I see him like immediately, like.

00:14:16.083 --> 00:14:17.507
- [Terry] He did it, he was like, oh.

00:14:17.507 --> 00:14:19.610
- But when he hears that horrible sound,

00:14:19.610 --> 00:14:20.810
you can't do that anymore.

00:14:20.810 --> 00:14:22.080
- [Heidi] Because they get scared,

00:14:22.080 --> 00:14:23.166
and then things can go wrong.

00:14:23.166 --> 00:14:24.807
- I wasn't thinking, I apologize.

00:14:24.807 --> 00:14:26.493
- [Terry] Oh, he lost
all his concentration.

00:14:26.493 --> 00:14:28.212
He was whipping like, oh wow.

00:14:28.212 --> 00:14:32.125
- Wasn't thinking, slash,
what would happen now?

00:14:32.125 --> 00:14:34.750
- We were like oh, whoa!

00:14:34.750 --> 00:14:36.360
- [Kelly] Terry, you have a new memoir.

00:14:36.360 --> 00:14:38.120
So did your family help
you at all with it?

00:14:38.120 --> 00:14:40.471
- Yes they did because
they're in it, like big-time.

00:14:40.471 --> 00:14:41.447
- [Kelly] Okay. Did you have?

00:14:41.447 --> 00:14:44.230
- And again, my kids were
like, oh my God, you told 'em

00:14:44.230 --> 00:14:45.184
about this, you told 'em about that.

00:14:45.184 --> 00:14:47.950
But first of all, I love the fact,

00:14:47.950 --> 00:14:52.605
I really like being transparent
because most men don't talk.

00:14:52.605 --> 00:14:53.438
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:14:53.438 --> 00:14:54.430
- We just don't talk to each other.

00:14:54.430 --> 00:14:56.390
And I said, man, we've got to be,

00:14:56.390 --> 00:14:59.245
I wanted to make sure people
didn't feel alone, you know?

00:14:59.245 --> 00:15:00.078
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:15:00.078 --> 00:15:01.883
- And especially the guys and
we talk about our own issues,

00:15:01.883 --> 00:15:04.490
the things we're going
through and just open up

00:15:04.490 --> 00:15:06.670
these conversations and it's so cathartic,

00:15:06.670 --> 00:15:07.710
and it felt so good.

00:15:07.710 --> 00:15:08.902
I think everybody in the world

00:15:08.902 --> 00:15:10.354
needs to write their own book so you can

00:15:10.354 --> 00:15:14.270
straighten out your values,
know where you stand.

00:15:14.270 --> 00:15:16.050
And it was just so much fun.

00:15:16.050 --> 00:15:17.740
- [Simon] By the way,
I'm not just saying this.

00:15:17.740 --> 00:15:19.890
I have started to read
it, it is brilliant.

00:15:19.890 --> 00:15:22.501
You've got to buy this book
and I really mean this.

00:15:22.501 --> 00:15:24.807
I'm not just saying this
'cause I was told to.

00:15:24.807 --> 00:15:27.420
- I love that you did it
with your family though,

00:15:27.420 --> 00:15:29.266
because that's kind of
true and they'll keep you,

00:15:29.266 --> 00:15:30.960
'cause sometimes I feel like your friends

00:15:30.960 --> 00:15:32.834
or your family almost know you
better than you do sometimes.

00:15:32.834 --> 00:15:33.667
- [Terry] Yeah.

00:15:33.667 --> 00:15:34.500
- Even if you're like the
most self-aware person.

00:15:34.500 --> 00:15:35.821
So that's really cool.

00:15:35.821 --> 00:15:36.654
- [Terry] Yeah.

00:15:36.654 --> 00:15:37.698
- And also a chance for them to be like,

00:15:37.698 --> 00:15:39.100
"No, that's not going in there."

00:15:39.100 --> 00:15:41.532
- Exactly, well, my wife will tell me,

00:15:41.532 --> 00:15:42.440
"No, that didn't happen.
You need to straighten

00:15:42.440 --> 00:15:43.340
that chapter out right now."

00:15:43.340 --> 00:15:44.465
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:15:44.465 --> 00:15:45.298
